Implement sort() method
----------------------------------------------------------
1. Method declaration
 -> Create the sort method inside DoubleLinkedList.java.
    It should accept a Comparator<T> as its argument.

2. Handle special cases
 -> If the list is empty or contains only one element,
    no sorting is necessary.

3. Start from head
 -> Use a walker to traverse the list, beginning at head.

4. Compare adjacent elements
 -> Compare the current node's item with the next node's
    item using the supplied Comparator.

5. Check the comparison result
 -> For ascending order, a positive comparison result means
    those two items are out of order.

6. Swap the items
 -> Exchange the stored items when necessary. Keep the actual
    nodes and their links unchanged.

7. Continue traversing
 -> Move to the next pair and continue until you reach the
    end of the list.

8. Repeat the process
 -> Perform additional passes until a complete pass finishes
    without any swaps.

9. Preserve your fingers
 -> Because you're swapping items rather than moving nodes,
    the finger references and their indices remain valid.

10. Test your method
 -> Test an unsorted list, already sorted list, reverse-sorted list,
    duplicate values, empty list, and one-element list.



